WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.250
Hi, I’m Ritesh. Let me show you how I build reliable AI.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.200
A task comes in. The planner picks a tool.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.300
Each observation feeds the next step.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.350
Deterministic checks verify the trace before the answer.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.100
Synthetic events stream through the pipeline.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.000
Rules flag fraud. A watermark drops very late events.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.650
Same logic as my Kafka, Spark and Cassandra project.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.400
MAREF: six reliability dimensions, not one score.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.400
Accuracy, grounding, hallucination, instructions, consistency, completion.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.950
In development: no results are claimed.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.200
RAG: real retrieval over a sample corpus.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.250
Chunks, scores and citations are all inspectable.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.550
Experimentation: real statistics decide ship or keep running.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.300
Funnels, retention and experiments.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.850
Every rate is an assumption you can change.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.600
Real-Time Streaming Pipeline

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.500
Spark Data Lakehouse

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.400
LLM Evaluation Framework

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.300
GenAI Document Assistant

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.200
MLOps Platform

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:35.950
Experimentation Toolkit

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.050
Let’s talk.
